@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-liquid-glass
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+The Deep Ocean background owner and Liquid Glass control plugin. Its Host half registers the `ui-liquid-glass` user-settings namespace. Its browser half owns one fixed `#dsh-liquid-background` Canvas, loads the shared Fluid asset, and contributes a compact panel to `sidebar.footer.action` plus a complete row to `settings.general.item`.
+
+The two controls share one reactive controller. Input changes repaint the Canvas and update Fluid parameters on the next animation frame, then coalesce Host writes for 180 ms. Reloads adopt `$DSH_HOME/settings.yaml`; remote or memory-mode browsers keep a process-local preference. Reset clears each user override so the deployment defaults become authoritative again.
+
+## Settings
+
+| Field | Default | Range or values | Effect |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `enabled` | `true` | boolean | Stops or resumes the Fluid animation loop. |
+| `opacity` | `48` | 0–100 | Canvas compositing opacity; light mode applies an additional readability reduction. |
+| `brightness` | `78` | 35–120 | Immediate display brightness for the cyan/blue dye. |
+| `flowSpeed` | `60` | 0–100 | Ambient current cadence and impulse. |
+| `pointerForce` | `55` | 0–100 | Pointer splat strength. |
+| `bloom` | `30` | 0–100 | Bloom intensity; zero removes the Bloom display keyword. |
+| `palette` | `ocean` | `abyss`, `ocean`, `cyan` | Bounded cyan-to-blue hue, saturation, and value ranges. |
+| `quality` | `balanced` | `eco`, `balanced`, `high` | Simulation, dye, pressure, and Bloom framebuffer workload. |
+
+Reduced Motion scales ambient motion and pointer force below the selected values. A hidden document or disabled surface has no active animation frame. Quality changes reuse the existing WebGL context and rebuild only its framebuffers. Plugin disposal removes the Canvas and script, clears timers and listeners, and asks `WEBGL_lose_context` to release GPU resources. WebGL or script failure leaves the static Deep Ocean gradient and all Harness controls usable.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+None, as the package changes browser presentation and user settings only; it does not alter session events, prompts, tools, or provider requests.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+None; the package never assembles model input.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- The Strong Refraction shader remains a separate progressive enhancement because DOM-background capture breaks overlay hit testing; these controls tune the shared Fluid source and CSS Glass materials only.
+- Palette changes affect newly injected dye while existing dye dissipates naturally, so the transition is gradual rather than an immediate framebuffer clear.
